		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">52</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">Following is what I come up with

We have 2 major phases in the implementation.
Phase 1: One is to read the pixels of image(i.e 1D array) and icon(i.e 1D array).
Phase 2: Second is count the number of times icon is appearing in the array

1. Read the length of 1D array from input(i.e. length of image).
2. Create an empty array (for storing pixels of image).
3. Read the next value from input
4. Append it to the array
5. Repeat steps 3 and 4 until you read all the elements of 1D array.
6. Read the length of 1D array from input(i.e. length of icon).
7. Create an empty array (for storing pixels of icon).
8. Read the next value from input
9. Append it to the array
10. Repeat steps 8 and 9 until you read all the elements of 1D array.
Phase 2
11. Create a variable called count and initialize it to 0 (for counting the number of times icons repeat in image).
12. Create a variable i and initialize it to 0.
13. Go to element with index i, of the image array and compare it with element at index 0, of icon array.
14. If both the elements are not equal then move to next element of image, otherwise,
14.1 Compare next element of image array to next element of icon array.
14.2 Repeat step 14.1 till you reach end of icon array.
15 We need to check if we came out of the loop because elements of the image and icon array elements are not equal or we reach the end of the icon array.
16. If we came out of the loop beacuse we reach end of icon array, then increase count value by 1, otherwise do nothing.
17. Go to the next element of image array by increasing the value of i by 1, or increase it by length of Icon array minus 1 if all pixels of Icon appears in Image array in same order.
18. Repeat steps 13, 14, 14.1, 14.2, 15, 16, 17 till we reach end of the image array.
19. Display the count value.</attribute>
